1
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:08,174
ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA - CUSTOMS OFFICER

2
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,968
Even if you keep nagging me like that…

3
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:12,011
It's not that I don't want to do it.

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,224
Come on, don't say that.
You're threatening me…

5
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:22,981
I'll call you back later
to discuss this. Bye.

6
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:25,275
Where did you come from?

7
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:27,527
The next flight will be arriving shortly.

8
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,904
Today, children on a field trip
are coming,

9
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:31,656
so we were told to do a thorough job.

10
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,950
I always do a thorough job.

11
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,144
He's getting grilled.

12
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,481
I wouldn't be able to take that.

13
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,857
You will inspect them,

14
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,109
every single one of them.
These are important to me.

15
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:11,321
This is Customs. What Customs does.

16
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:13,615
-is finding things that must not
-You all have things

17
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,492
-be brought into Japan.
-you keep by your side, right?

18
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,451
-Where?
-Fine.

19
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,079
Why are you coming now?

20
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,580
I didn't mean to!

21
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:24,250
What is he doing?

22
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,335
Are you getting scolded?

23
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,629
-Do what you want!
-I am not getting scolded.

24
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:28,671
You look kind of lame.

25
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:31,633
Not all adult jobs are cool.

26
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:33,259
‎Fine, fine. Go ahead!

27
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,094
Um…

28
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:38,807
He's fighting so that he can conduct
an important inspection…

29
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:41,518
-…for us.
-He's fighting?

30
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,353
-Yes.
-God, What a day!

31
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,189
-You got this!
-I had a bad feeling about today.

32
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:49,025
-You got this!
-You got this!

33
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:53,154
From the moment I woke up,
I had a bad feeling about today!

34
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:54,989
You got this!

35
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,491
This is chaos.

36
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,535
-You got this!
-You got this!

37
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:01,871
-You got this!
-You got this!

38
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,628
You and I spent two hours

39
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:11,256
checking the contents
of 42 USB flash drives.

40
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:13,550
I'm completely exhausted.

41
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:15,635
So, did anything come up?

42
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:17,262
Yes, something did.

43
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:19,472
Videos and photos he took
of his three growing children.

44
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,182
Family photos?

45
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,434
During the clip of his
daughter's piano recital,

46
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:26,104
that huge guy watched it
with us and was tearing up.

47
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:28,231
It was a waste of effort.

48
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:32,902
But sometimes people smuggle in data
hidden in those videos. It's quite common.

49
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,280
Yes. Yes!

50
00:02:35,363 --> 00:02:37,949
What do they call them again…

51
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:40,410
-Cold wallets?
-Cold wallets, yes, that's it!

52
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,662
The thing they use to hide crypto profits
to dodge taxes.

53
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:43,705
It's important work.

54
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:45,790
Because Immigration
won't do it themselves.

55
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:49,878
Our work isn't manual labor.
It's to, you know…

56
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:52,046
-Mental labor.
-It's mental labor.

57
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:58,094
-Is that all?
-Yes.

58
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:02,056
Are you feeling okay?

59
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:40,929
Shibuya Scramble Crossing.

60
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:45,141
And, and, and ramen!
I really, really have to try it.

61
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,643
I'm glad to hear that.

62
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:49,646
However, it's best
not to make jokes like that.

63
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,731
Sometimes they aren't
taken as jokes. Go ahead.

64
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:53,650
Sorry.

65
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:57,779
Is this all of your luggage?
Please let me inspect it.

66
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,200
Thank you.

67
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:05,328
He's so by the book.
He can't even take a joke.

68
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:08,790
I agree, he's a hardass.

69
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:12,043
However, we are not here to have
casual conversation with customers.

70
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:13,628
I know. It's just that

71
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:17,840
coming to Japan has been
my dream for so long.

72
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:22,095
But, yeah, I guess
I got a little bit carried away.

73
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,764
-Go ahead.
-Thank you.

74
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,684
-Excuse me. Could I see one more thing?
-Huh?

75
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:31,396
-May I see that necklace?
-Oh, yes.

76
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:34,357
-Here you go.
-Thank you very much.

77
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:40,571
-This is soil inside, right?
-Yes.

78
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,617
I'm sorry, but it will
have to be confiscated.

79
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,119
Confiscated?

80
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:49,372
You cannot bring
foreign soil into the country.

81
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,208
What? Even just a tiny amount?

82
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,794
It's prohibited, regardless of the amount.

83
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:57,672
I really like it.

84
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:01,092
I'm sorry, I'm quite by the book myself.

85
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:05,138
-It's okay. I get it.
-Thank you very much.

86
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,266
Plant Protection, please.

87
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:12,562
Is this okay?

88
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:16,482
Yes. Thank you very much.

89
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:20,820
-Am I free to go now?
-Of course.

90
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:24,449
Which means I'm free to go as well.

91
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:28,244
-Just this way, please.
-Okay.

92
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:30,413
Hayami, do you cook?

93
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,790
Yes, I do.

94
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:34,834
Really? What can you make?

95
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,713
-Pasta and stuff.
-Pasta? Wow…

96
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:40,131
-I'll be leaving now.
-See you.

97
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:41,215
Are you leaving already?

98
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:44,218
I was thinking of getting dinner
since my wife isn't home.

99
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:45,178
Care to join me?

100
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,180
I'm sorry. Not today.

101
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,515
-I see.
-Goodbye.

102
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:51,184
Bye.

103
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:54,020
Pasta is nice…

104
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:56,314
What kinds of pasta are you good at?

105
00:05:56,397 --> 00:06:00,068
-Well, I guess Roman pasta…
-Roman pasta!? That's…

106
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:01,569
Hayami, is that…

107
00:06:03,362 --> 00:06:06,324
No wonder he turned down my invitation.

108
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,077
By the way, Hayami,

109
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,995
-I'd like to try your--
-I'm sorry.

110
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,288
I'm also busy today.

111
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:16,834
I see.

112
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:26,511
-Good morning.
-Morning.

113
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:30,473
What's happening?

114
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,352
Everyone's here.

115
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:38,523
This is Nishida
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

116
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,316
I'm Nishida from the First Division.

117
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:44,070
He's here to ask about the murder case
that occurred last night.

118
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,404
Murder case?

119
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:48,741
The name of the murdered victim
is Amita Barad.

120
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,076
She was a female university student

121
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:52,787
-who arrived from the Republic of Chatwan.
-Amita Barad…

122
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:53,871
Her!

123
00:06:58,042 --> 00:07:01,671
Given the short time between the victim's
entry into the country and the incident,

124
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:04,549
it's possible the perpetrator
followed her from the airport.

125
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:06,634
I'd like to ask about her entry.

126
00:07:06,717 --> 00:07:09,929
Of course, we won't hesitate
to cooperate with the police.

127
00:07:10,012 --> 00:07:11,097
Thank you very much.

128
00:07:12,181 --> 00:07:13,433
Well then, you.

129
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:15,935
What, me?

130
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:18,855
Actually, this was found
on the victim's smartphone.

131
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:28,531
‎Oh my…

132
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:32,452
You and the victim
had never met before that point.

133
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:35,163
Is that correct?

134
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:37,540
Yes.

135
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:42,670
And yet, the victim had a picture of you.

136
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:43,838
Why is that?

137
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:45,256
Well…

138
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:48,509
I don't know. I have no idea.

139
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,303
I see…

140
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,348
But isn't that strange?

141
00:07:57,018 --> 00:08:00,730
"The body found in a park in Suginami Ward
in the early hours of the morning

142
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,315
was identified as 25-year-old Amita Barad,

143
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:04,525
a traveler from the Republic of Chatwan."

144
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:07,361
To think this would happen
to that woman who entered yesterday.

145
00:08:07,445 --> 00:08:11,324
Suginami Ward isn't an unsafe area either.

146
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:13,743
Still, it's not really
a place tourists go to.

147
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:15,745
Maybe she had an acquaintance there.

148
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:18,206
She didn't seem like she was going
to meet an acquaintance, though.

149
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:22,251
-Why is that?
-She was eager to do sightseeing.

150
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:25,546
But she also said something alarming.

151
00:08:28,132 --> 00:08:31,636
She joked that she came here
to smuggle drugs.

152
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,262
Smuggle?

153
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,899
-How did it go?
-What did he ask you?

154
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:46,692
Nothing much, really.

155
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,778
She's the girl
you were with yesterday, right?

156
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,240
-Yes.
-What's with her having a photo

157
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,325
-of you on her phone?
-Well…

158
00:08:54,992 --> 00:08:57,286
How should I know?

159
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,163
I'm going to the inspection booth.

160
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,164
Okay.

161
00:09:05,169 --> 00:09:09,257
It must be a shock, having someone
you inspected end up like that.

162
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:14,011
Do you think what she said
was really just a joke?

163
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:27,775
DO NOT ENTER

164
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:43,416
-Was Matsuyama really called in again?
-Yes.

165
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:47,003
They want to double-check something with
Matsuyama since he inspected her luggage.

166
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:48,296
But why?

167
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:51,090
-This time, those two came as well.
-Those two?

168
00:09:51,173 --> 00:09:53,342
Inspector Iuchi
and Assistant Inspector Nakatsuka.

169
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,136
Those two aren't from the First Division.

170
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:57,179
They are from
the International Crime Division.

171
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,389
-Right?
-Yes.

172
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:02,393
The First Investigation Division
and the International Crime Division…

173
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:06,731
It's strange.

174
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:09,734
You take the train when commuting
to and from here, don't you?

175
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:13,946
But the station is in the opposite
direction from that bus stop.

176
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:17,325
Why did you go over there?

177
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:21,829
I had plans to meet an acquaintance
that day, so I didn't take the train.

178
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:26,834
So, on that day of all days, you didn't
use the train, walked to the bus stop,

179
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:28,586
and happened to run into her.

180
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:32,381
That's a remarkably convenient story.

181
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:35,301
That happens to be the truth,
so what choice do I have?

182
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:36,761
What exactly are you trying to say?

183
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:41,891
You knew the victim beforehand,
didn't you?

184
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:49,940
I have nothing more to say to you.

185
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,108
Excuse me.

186
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:56,989
We're not finished talking.

187
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,034
Sit down.

188
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:07,500
Why do we have to wait
in a place like this?

189
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:10,211
What choice do we have? He always
wants to do everything by himself.

190
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:12,296
Are we just sidekicks?

191
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,383
Is Division One really that special?

192
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:24,058
What is it?

193
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:27,311
Why are you interrogating
Matsuyama multiple times?

194
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:29,146
It's not an interrogation.
We're just talking.

195
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,564
Isn't that the same thing?

196
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:33,692
No, we can't disclose
investigation details.

197
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:37,071
Now, now, don't be so rigid.
We're practically friends, detectives.

198
00:11:37,154 --> 00:11:39,240
I don't recall becoming friends with you.

199
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,742
Then how about we become friends now?

200
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,496
‎What?

201
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:47,790
Wait…

202
00:11:47,873 --> 00:11:50,626
-You hear what she's saying?
-Idiot.

203
00:11:58,676 --> 00:11:59,510
Scary.

204
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:03,639
The two detectives said that if
Matsuyama and Amita knew each other,

205
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,850
they wanted to know the reason why.

206
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,184
What do you mean?

207
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:10,646
This is strange.

208
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:12,815
What is this?

209
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,401
This is the footage
from Amita's immigration inspection.

210
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:20,781
GATE 24 - IN FRONT OF BOOTH A &amp; B

211
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,450
What about it?

212
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:24,660
Neither booth had a line,

213
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:27,204
yet she hesitated about
which one to go to.

214
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,497
Now that you mention it…

215
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,417
After that, she looked up
something on her smartphone.

216
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,044
Ah, she's comparing the photo
on her phone with Matsuyama.

217
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:38,382
Is it possible she chose Matsuyama
specifically to undergo inspection?

218
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:40,217
She chose Matsuyama? What does that mean?

219
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:42,011
I don't know.

220
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:45,014
Well, from the police's perspective,

221
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:49,018
it looks like she thought
Matsuyama would turn a blind eye

222
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:51,270
to whatever she was carrying in, right?

223
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,856
Does that mean…

224
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,649
Smuggling?

225
00:12:56,984 --> 00:13:00,321
But Matsuyama confiscated
her necklace, didn't he?

226
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:01,989
Yes, however…

227
00:13:02,072 --> 00:13:03,073
However?

228
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,825
However,

229
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:08,537
it could have been a camouflage
to let something else pass through.

230
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,873
That is likely what
the police are suspicious of.

231
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:14,752
Amita brought something in
with Matsuyama's assistance.

232
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:17,630
Which led to her being killed.

233
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,673
Is that what you mean?

234
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:23,802
When viewed that way, it explains why
the First Investigation Division

235
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,846
and International Crime Division
are taking action.

236
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,307
-Um…
-Hm?

237
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:30,226
Ah, never mind.

238
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:32,228
Do speak up. Anything is fine.

239
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:38,692
I saw something.

240
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:02,466
Come to think of it, he hasn't
been very sociable lately.

241
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:04,176
He turned down my invitation too…

242
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,719
I don't think that has
anything to do with this.

243
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,846
Ouch, that hit right where it hurts.

244
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:09,640
Still,

245
00:14:09,723 --> 00:14:13,561
isn't it premature to assume
Matsuyama committed misconduct?

246
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:15,062
Even though he was given money?

247
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:19,066
As a bribery case, it's picture-perfect.

248
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,278
What do you think, Mori?

249
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:29,994
I can't say for sure

250
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:31,996
without physical evidence.

251
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:38,752
It's from Matsuyama.

252
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:42,423
He says he's heading straight home
due to feeling unwell.

253
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:46,093
Being interrogated repeatedly
would do that to anyone.

254
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:51,140
He's off duty tomorrow, right?

255
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,239
I'm sorry for dragging you
into this on your day off.

256
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,784
No, not at all. I tagged along on my own.

257
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:13,287
Tailing someone is too heavy
a task for Machi.

258
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:16,749
Honestly, it could just be me and you.

259
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:18,667
I've never tailed anyone before.

260
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,252
Me neither.

261
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:21,337
But

262
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:25,049
you said you didn't want to leave
questions unanswered, right?

263
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,675
Yes.

264
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,385
Then we have no choice but to investigate.

265
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:31,305
But would someone suspected
of being an accomplice to smuggling

266
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:34,224
meet with a member
of a smuggling ring in broad daylight?

267
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,853
Thanks for waiting.

268
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:41,440
-You can sit over there.
-I'm meeting with him here.

269
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,988
Wait, wait! What are you doing?

270
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,031
Come here.

271
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,286
-I'm going to talk to him.
-What?

272
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,956
We just need to hear
the truth directly from him.

273
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:59,875
He looks dangerous! What if
something happens to you?

274
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:05,589
You can let go of me now.

275
00:16:06,423 --> 00:16:08,550
-No.
-What?

276
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:12,596
Hey.

277
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:24,692
-Matsuyama.
-Yes?

278
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,077
Who is this man?

279
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,122
Were you following me?

280
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,165
That's quite malicious of you.

281
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:44,878
Endo saw you
receiving money from this man.

282
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:48,424
So that gives you
the right to snoop around?

283
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,175
No, Matsuyama,

284
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,052
we just want to know the truth.

285
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,595
The truth?

286
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:58,726
That I took money from this man
and overlooked smuggling?

287
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:00,644
Did you?

288
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:03,814
This man is…

289
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:07,484
Um, the detectives are here again.

290
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:09,570
-What do you want now?
-I obtained authorization.

291
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:13,449
I checked your travel history.

292
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:16,493
You visited Chatwan, the victim's
homeland, last year, didn't you?

293
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:20,456
Maybe you met her over there?

294
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:24,043
Why don't you let us hear the details?

295
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:28,756
Cut it out.

296
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:33,677
‎Ow, ow, ow…

297
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:38,849
Obstruction of official duties.

298
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:43,604
An airport customs officer

299
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,273
was arrested under suspicion
of being an accomplice to smuggling.

300
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:47,524
This is unprecedented.

301
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:48,859
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM
MIDORI SUGIHARA

302
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:52,029
Why does Gate 24 keep
bringing one trouble after another?

303
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:54,198
He hasn't been arrested.

304
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,699
He was merely taken in for questioning.

305
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,284
He was handcuffed, wasn't he?

306
00:17:57,367 --> 00:18:00,245
That was the detective acting out of line.

307
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:02,748
Matsuyama has already been released.

308
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:07,252
The smartphone photo,
security camera footage, travel history…

309
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,630
With this much circumstantial evidence
lined up,

310
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:11,548
an arrest is only a matter of time.

311
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:14,510
Counselor,

312
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:17,346
you should take action
before this escalates further.

313
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:20,849
However, there is also the principle

314
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,893
-of innocent until proven guilty.
-How naive.

315
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:24,561
An error in judgment

316
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:27,397
could become an issue
concerning the survival of Gate 24.

317
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:31,819
Acknowledging that there was
an offender within the team

318
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:34,988
you personally created must be painful,

319
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:37,199
but shouldn't you make
a wise decision here?

320
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:49,795
U-u-um…

321
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,840
We were worried.

322
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,508
Are you all right?

323
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,635
Yes.

324
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:04,434
This man
is a high school classmate of mine.

325
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,353
A classmate?

326
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,856
-Oh my…
-That rough-looking guy?

327
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:11,859
Even if he looks rough,
he's far more successful than me.

328
00:19:11,942 --> 00:19:14,153
He started a venture business
right out of high school,

329
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:16,363
and now he's a CEO
with annual revenue of a billion yen.

330
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,031
Annual revenue of a billion yen?

331
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:18,949
CEO…

332
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,201
Then what I saw was…

333
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:26,456
It was probably him trying to pay me back
for a meal I paid for him previously.

334
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:28,500
Hey, that's too much.

335
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,377
Huh? Oh…

336
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:33,005
I turned it down,
but he forced it into my hand.

337
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:35,090
But you were handed a stack of bills.

338
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:38,051
A stack of bills?
It was 20,000 yen at most.

339
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,179
-Here.
-Ah, thank you.

340
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:43,223
-It wasn't a stack of bills!
-I'm sorry!

341
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:44,558
He's a genuinely good guy,

342
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:48,312
and he keeps inviting me to work with him.

343
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,064
-Work together with him?
-And quitting this job?

344
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:52,232
Why?

345
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:54,234
You've been working so hard.

346
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,235
Are you dissatisfied here?

347
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:57,196
You used to grumble that
non-career staff can't move up,

348
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,740
-but that's not the case anymore.
-It's not about that.

349
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:05,287
You're fluent in English
and good with people,

350
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:08,081
so you're perfect
for doing sales overseas.

351
00:20:08,957 --> 00:20:12,002
But I like the airport,

352
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:13,670
and I like this job.

353
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:16,840
You like it?

354
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:21,845
Your job is opening people's luggage
and taking away bad stuff, right?

355
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,556
With everyone angry at you.

356
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:28,602
Angry at me, huh…

357
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:33,065
Is that a job only you can do?

358
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:37,361
Let's do something together
that only you can do.

359
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,035
I thought about it.

360
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:49,039
The suitcases of people on those planes

361
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:51,124
are stuffed with dreams.

362
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:54,419
She was like that too.

363
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:59,091
-Oh, Mr. By-the-Book.
-Hello.

364
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:02,761
Is this a coincidence, or did you come
to give me back my necklace?

365
00:21:02,844 --> 00:21:04,638
Unfortunately, it's a coincidence.

366
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:05,889
Aw, too bad.

367
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,892
That reminds me.

368
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:11,061
I went to your country
as a tourist last year.

369
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,104
It was a wonderful country.

370
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,855
-Really?
-Yes.

371
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:16,692
But Japan is a wonderful country as well.

372
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:18,610
Yes, that's true.

373
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,279
I'm only here for a week,

374
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:24,032
but I'm going to share everything
I see and hear on social media.

375
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:28,161
I just want people back home
to see how great Japan is.

376
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:30,998
Thank you very much. Enjoy yourself.

377
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,041
Welcome to Japan.

378
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,753
But what about myself?

379
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,339
Paying attention

380
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:42,009
to other people's belongings here,

381
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,136
while grinding my nerves down…

382
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,972
I started to worry that I was losing

383
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:50,767
important things,
like my own dreams and hopes.

384
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:58,191
Hello. This is Seike.

385
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:00,569
Yes.

386
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:06,241
Matsuyama. The Counselor
is calling for you.

387
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:24,885
Counselor Sugihara has decided
to suspend Matsuyama for the time being.

388
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:27,763
-Really?
-Because you two made a fuss out of it.

389
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:29,097
Hold on now.

390
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:31,767
The fact that he was released
is thanks to us.

391
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:34,728
Yes. We're having a hard time
dealing with Nishida ourselves.

392
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:35,687
That's right.

393
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:38,356
He hasn't had any remarkable
results lately, so he's getting impatient.

394
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:42,069
Then he came into our territory
to get a smuggling and murder case.

395
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:43,779
He's a real piece of work.

396
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:47,032
That 43-year-old man makes my blood boil.

397
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:49,785
Is it fine to speak so freely
about your colleague's personal matters?

398
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:51,620
This isn't personal information.

399
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:53,955
It's badmouthing.

400
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,084
-Neither is okay.
-Oh…

401
00:22:57,876 --> 00:22:58,835
Um…

402
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:03,715
May I ask one thing?

403
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:08,178
What did Amita bring in?

404
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:11,932
Security cameras at the hotel
where the victim checked in

405
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:14,351
showed her leaving the hotel

406
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:16,436
holding a paper shopping bag.

407
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:22,484
However, that paper bag wasn't at the park
so we think the perpetrator took it.

408
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:26,822
This is a photo of her suitcase.

409
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:35,997
It looks as though something
has been removed entirely.

410
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:38,875
She probably took whatever
was stored there with her.

411
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:43,839
Is this suitcase size medium or large?

412
00:23:47,342 --> 00:23:49,261
Roughly about this big, I suppose.

413
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:51,096
In that case, it's a medium.

414
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:53,515
An M-size suitcase is generally

415
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:56,685
66 cm tall, 44 cm wide,

416
00:23:56,768 --> 00:23:58,770
and 27 cm deep.

417
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:01,231
Estimating the blank space
from those dimensions,

418
00:24:01,314 --> 00:24:06,111
it's about 19 cm tall, 14 cm wide,
and 10 cm deep.

419
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:07,821
Something like this.

420
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:09,406
What is that?

421
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:11,324
I wonder. Some kind of box?

422
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:14,411
Some kind of book, perhaps?
Like a dictionary.

423
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:17,455
Who brings a paper dictionary
on a trip nowadays?

424
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:22,252
If it were a hardcover book,
it would be 20 cm tall and 15 cm wide.

425
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:25,672
It's close, but book sizes
vary by country.

426
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,258
Or perhaps…

427
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,475
-A DVD?
-Yes.

428
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:41,146
DVD cases are a universal size.

429
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:44,399
Nineteen cm tall and 13 cm wide.

430
00:24:44,482 --> 00:24:48,278
A DVD box set fits perfectly into
the square space of Amita's suitcase.

431
00:24:48,361 --> 00:24:50,822
Do you remember if there was
something like that in the suitcase?

432
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:56,077
Now that you mention it, a DVD set…

433
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:57,329
It was there, right?

434
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:59,581
I only vaguely remember,

435
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:03,919
but it looked like a romance, with a man
and a woman staring at each other.

436
00:25:04,002 --> 00:25:05,837
A man and a woman staring at each other…

437
00:25:06,546 --> 00:25:10,842
But after that, my focus
was taken up by her necklace.

438
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:11,968
Ah, really…

439
00:25:12,552 --> 00:25:14,846
The soil in that necklace
really caught your eye, huh?

440
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:20,268
I noticed it because I'd confiscated
the same necklace in the past. I think…

441
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:21,978
The same necklace?

442
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:23,396
Yes.

443
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:28,902
The same customs officer
confiscated the same necklace.

444
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:31,738
Is that just a coincidence?

445
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:41,748
This is a record of the necklace
Matsuyama previously confiscated.

446
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:43,124
Utsugi, nice play!

447
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:45,961
This is the necklace
confiscated from Amita.

448
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:47,837
Yes, they are identical.

449
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:51,174
Hana Chaplan. She was also from Chatwan.

450
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:53,718
What is she doing now?

451
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:55,762
What do you mean?

452
00:25:55,845 --> 00:25:57,472
Well, do you think

453
00:25:57,555 --> 00:26:00,267
the same thing that happened to Amita
could have happened to her?

454
00:26:01,643 --> 00:26:03,103
I'll check the entry and exit records.

455
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:08,566
I feel like I've seen
this necklace somewhere…

456
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:14,739
Oh my.

457
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:23,290
This is a DVD of a romance drama that
enjoyed immense popularity in Chatwan.

458
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:26,251
It's a story where a pilot
injured in an accident

459
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:28,253
and a flight attendant engaged

460
00:26:28,336 --> 00:26:30,213
to a wealthy tycoon reunite
on a hill of memories

461
00:26:30,297 --> 00:26:32,507
at the end of the drama
and reclaim their love.

462
00:26:32,590 --> 00:26:35,135
So cliché. But I love that kind of stuff.

463
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:36,261
Huh?

464
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:40,056
You didn't know Korean idols,
but you're well-versed in Chatwan dramas?

465
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:43,059
Yes. I learned from the Korean idols case,
so I studied up.

466
00:26:43,143 --> 00:26:45,270
Is that drama connected
to the necklace in some way?

467
00:26:45,895 --> 00:26:46,938
Yes.

468
00:26:48,023 --> 00:26:52,152
This necklace is a bonus item
that comes with purchasing the DVD set.

469
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:54,279
-A bonus item?
-Yes.

470
00:26:54,362 --> 00:26:57,615
And the soil inside this bottle

471
00:26:58,283 --> 00:27:00,618
is from this hill of memories.

472
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:03,747
I found her.

473
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:06,416
Hana Chaplan, 25 years old.
She's still in the country.

474
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:14,549
Hana Chaplan was a college student
who came to Japan as a monitor

475
00:27:14,632 --> 00:27:16,593
to post about her stay
in Japan on social media.

476
00:27:16,676 --> 00:27:21,181
It seems she had all
travel expenses to Japan paid for.

477
00:27:21,264 --> 00:27:23,641
However, there was a condition.

478
00:27:24,225 --> 00:27:25,268
A condition?

479
00:27:30,106 --> 00:27:32,734
When you arrive in Japan, I want you
to hand this to a friend of mine.

480
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:35,653
Is there something wrong with that?

481
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:38,782
Of course not.
You know this drama too, right?

482
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,825
My friend wants to watch it.

483
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:45,121
This is a bonus item you get
when you buy the set.

484
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:47,207
-Put it on.
-Thank you.

485
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:51,920
It would be troublesome if those DVDs
got confiscated at customs by mistake,

486
00:27:52,003 --> 00:27:53,838
so make sure to go through
inspection with that man.

487
00:27:54,547 --> 00:27:57,967
Amita likely received
the same instruction.

488
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,803
What is in that DVD?

489
00:27:59,886 --> 00:28:01,596
I thought maybe it was something

490
00:28:01,679 --> 00:28:05,433
available only over there, traded
at high prices as a collector's item.

491
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:08,436
It was not something
with that kind of value.

492
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,437
I see.

493
00:28:11,147 --> 00:28:13,733
So you all looked into this.

494
00:28:13,817 --> 00:28:16,319
Yes. As you can see,
we haven't neglected our duties.

495
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,406
It's just frustrating, isn't it?

496
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:23,618
We can lift Matsuyama's
suspension now, right?

497
00:28:26,246 --> 00:28:28,873
He submitted his resignation.

498
00:28:33,586 --> 00:28:36,756
He submitted his resignation.

499
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:41,594
He said that as a customs officer
suspected of aiding in smuggling,

500
00:28:41,678 --> 00:28:44,556
he can't continue doing the job.

501
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:48,184
Matsuyama

502
00:28:48,935 --> 00:28:51,104
hasn't done anything wrong, though.

503
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:53,398
Yes.

504
00:28:53,481 --> 00:28:58,486
However, Amita and Hana were instructed
to go through Matsuyama's booth

505
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:00,488
and were given his photo.

506
00:29:01,614 --> 00:29:04,159
Unless the reason for that becomes clear,

507
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:06,077
the suspicion surrounding him
won't be cleared.

508
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:07,954
In that case, we should
find that out as well.

509
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:19,048
This is the photo of Matsuyama
that Hana and Amita received.

510
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:20,633
That's our booth.

511
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:21,968
Photography is prohibited there.

512
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,887
-They must have taken it secretly.
-Yes.

513
00:29:23,970 --> 00:29:26,639
It's during shift hours.
He's standing there blankly.

514
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:27,682
True.

515
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:31,102
Judging from the angle,
it was taken from in front of the exit.

516
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:36,024
If an arriving passenger is in the photo,
we might be able to identify the flight.

517
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:38,485
Is there any benefit
to knowing the flight?

518
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,320
We'll know what day this photo was taken.

519
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:42,238
I see. If we know the date and time,

520
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:44,365
we can identify the photographer
using CCTV.

521
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:46,659
Um…

522
00:29:49,078 --> 00:29:50,705
What is this?

523
00:29:52,707 --> 00:29:53,666
Fabric?

524
00:29:55,001 --> 00:29:55,919
Clothing?

525
00:29:57,962 --> 00:30:00,924
Isn't this a hat?

526
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:04,344
At this height, a child?

527
00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:06,012
An elementary school student.

528
00:30:06,095 --> 00:30:09,307
An elementary school student
with a white hat…

529
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:16,523
-The field trip!
-The field trip!

530
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:19,776
The students from Akikasho Elementary
came on a field trip

531
00:30:19,859 --> 00:30:23,822
on June 29th, from 1:00 p.m. to 1:30 p.m.

532
00:30:28,451 --> 00:30:29,619
It's this man.

533
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:31,704
Hold on, hold on.

534
00:30:32,288 --> 00:30:35,208
It's not all good, you know.

535
00:30:35,792 --> 00:30:38,002
She received instructions

536
00:30:38,086 --> 00:30:40,880
and did something dangerous.

537
00:30:46,177 --> 00:30:47,595
Sorry to bother you.

538
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,097
We're the police.

539
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:53,017
PREPARING

540
00:30:53,101 --> 00:30:55,353
You took this photo, didn't you?

541
00:30:55,436 --> 00:30:59,232
Your boss had a villa in Chatwan, right?

542
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:00,900
What were you doing,
using that villa as a base?

543
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:02,861
I don't know anything.
I'm not a gang member.

544
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:05,697
You were waiting in a black car
for the boss to return, weren't you?

545
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:07,740
You're basically a member.

546
00:31:09,325 --> 00:31:12,704
The woman who had this photo
on her smartphone was murdered.

547
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:15,456
You're already involved in this.

548
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:18,126
-I don't know anything about a murder!
-Then what do you know?

549
00:31:18,209 --> 00:31:19,419
-Sit down. Come on.
-No,

550
00:31:19,502 --> 00:31:21,963
-You took the photo!
-I don't know anything!

551
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:22,881
No,

552
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:24,716
-I didn't do anything…
-What are you doing here?

553
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:25,925
May I have a moment?

554
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:28,136
Sit tight.

555
00:31:28,845 --> 00:31:30,013
What is it?

556
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:33,308
Um, do you always do things like this?

557
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:36,060
Well, yes. Don't like it?

558
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:38,146
We're doing this for all your sakes.

559
00:31:38,229 --> 00:31:40,315
-Well, that's enough then.
-What?

560
00:31:54,787 --> 00:31:55,830
What are you doing?

561
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:58,958
-I'm looking at your eyes.
-My eyes?

562
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:04,631
Because of my job,

563
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:08,509
I look at the eyes of people
from many different countries.

564
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:14,641
Among them, very rarely,
there are people with eyes like yours.

565
00:32:16,684 --> 00:32:18,019
What kind of eyes?

566
00:32:18,603 --> 00:32:20,939
Eyes wavering between good and evil.

567
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:25,151
The eyes of someone standing
on the edge of a cliff.

568
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:31,824
Because of the photo you took,

569
00:32:33,117 --> 00:32:34,285
a woman lost her life,

570
00:32:36,287 --> 00:32:38,498
and a man was thrown off
the tracks of his life.

571
00:32:39,540 --> 00:32:42,460
You can't get back her life.
That mistake won't go away.

572
00:32:42,961 --> 00:32:46,631
But right now, it's still possible
to save a man's life.

573
00:32:50,009 --> 00:32:51,427
The only one who can do that

574
00:32:52,553 --> 00:32:53,721
is you.

575
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:02,939
All right,

576
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:04,607
Detective.

577
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,986
-Okay.
-Amazing…

578
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:10,113
Here you go.

579
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,700
Sorry it's not katsudon.

580
00:33:14,742 --> 00:33:15,910
Thank you.

581
00:33:17,036 --> 00:33:19,372
He's not a detective, though.

582
00:33:19,455 --> 00:33:21,666
It seems that man

583
00:33:22,583 --> 00:33:26,587
looked into the customs officers
at Gate 24

584
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:28,798
for the smuggling.

585
00:33:30,049 --> 00:33:32,051
He looked into the customs officers?

586
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:33,886
Not many flights come from Chatwan,

587
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:37,140
so they always enter through that gate.

588
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:41,185
The officers gathered at a newly built,
isolated gate like that

589
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:45,565
are just a ragtag group,
and inspections are lax.

590
00:33:45,648 --> 00:33:49,402
I was instructed to pick the one who
seemed especially lax and send a photo.

591
00:33:49,485 --> 00:33:51,446
And the one chosen

592
00:33:51,529 --> 00:33:54,282
was Matsuyama, who was the youngest
and seemed the most good-natured.

593
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:57,243
He wasn't an accomplice.

594
00:33:57,326 --> 00:33:58,578
He was a victim.

595
00:33:59,078 --> 00:34:01,414
A ragtag group with lax inspections.

596
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:04,292
They really were taking us for fools, huh.

597
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:10,590
I reported this to Detective Nishida
to clear his suspicion.

598
00:34:11,382 --> 00:34:13,176
Then a proposal came from their side.

599
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:17,263
We obtained information that a woman

600
00:34:17,346 --> 00:34:20,850
carrying that DVD
is on the next flight from Chatwan.

601
00:34:21,642 --> 00:34:22,685
So,

602
00:34:22,769 --> 00:34:25,313
we want you to let that woman
enter the country.

603
00:34:26,522 --> 00:34:27,857
Why me?

604
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:31,986
She has been instructed
to undergo inspection by you.

605
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:34,781
Just like with Amita.

606
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:38,701
The one who killed her is almost certainly
the person receiving the DVD.

607
00:34:38,785 --> 00:34:40,828
We'll have the woman
guide us to that person.

608
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:44,499
You're telling me to send
a woman to a murderer?

609
00:34:44,582 --> 00:34:47,126
We will do everything possible
to ensure her safety.

610
00:34:47,835 --> 00:34:50,379
We want to catch the killer
no matter what.

611
00:34:50,463 --> 00:34:52,757
You feel the same, don't you?

612
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:57,136
‎GATE 24 - SECONDARY ROOMGATE 24
‎SECONDARY ROOM

613
00:35:27,750 --> 00:35:29,627
‎GATE 24 - IN FRONT OF BOOTH A &amp; B

614
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:33,381
Mori, what are you doing?

615
00:35:33,464 --> 00:35:36,175
-I'm investigating.
-Investigating what?

616
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:38,052
It's been bothering me.

617
00:35:38,636 --> 00:35:42,849
Why is the smuggling group trying to bring
in the same DVD over and over again?

618
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:50,064
I don't want to leave
questions unanswered.

619
00:36:10,334 --> 00:36:11,169
She's here.

620
00:36:24,932 --> 00:36:26,517
Oh my…

621
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:31,355
-Your passport, please.
-Here you go.

622
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:40,698
-Please proceed to baggage check.
-Okay.

623
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:43,659
May I see inside?

624
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:48,414
Here.

625
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:02,929
What is this?

626
00:37:03,971 --> 00:37:07,600
It's a DVD set.
A famous drama from my country.

627
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:11,646
Really? Understood.

628
00:37:19,153 --> 00:37:21,656
-I will inspect the inside of this again.
-Okay.

629
00:37:22,281 --> 00:37:23,241
What are you doing?

630
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:26,661
-This DVD might contain steganography.
-What?

631
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:29,247
It's an information-hiding method
where other data

632
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:30,831
is embedded inside recorded data.

633
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:40,675
This DVD has been altered…

634
00:37:42,718 --> 00:37:44,262
and the light reflection is unusual.

635
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:46,138
Hey.

636
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:47,765
What are you doing?

637
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:49,850
‎This one too.

638
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:51,519
What's going on?

639
00:37:51,602 --> 00:37:53,354
This DVD has other information

640
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:55,356
-hidden on it.
-Mori, that's enough.

641
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,947
There's no problem. Go ahead.

642
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:04,198
That way, please.

643
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:05,658
‎Thank you.

644
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:10,871
Matsuyama.

645
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:13,040
Are you okay with this?

646
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:18,421
What is our job?

647
00:38:21,132 --> 00:38:22,383
Our

648
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:23,843
job?

649
00:38:39,692 --> 00:38:41,652
You cannot bring those DVDs in!

650
00:38:42,194 --> 00:38:43,904
I'm confiscating them.

651
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:46,741
What is he doing!?

652
00:38:47,950 --> 00:38:49,452
What? Why?

653
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:54,790
It has information that is prohibited
from being taken out of your country.

654
00:38:55,374 --> 00:38:58,252
What are you talking about?
That's impossible.

655
00:38:58,336 --> 00:39:00,588
You were asked to hand this DVD

656
00:39:00,671 --> 00:39:03,215
over to a certain person.

657
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,593
How do you know about that?

658
00:39:07,303 --> 00:39:11,098
There was a woman who came
from Chatwan just like you.

659
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:13,059
But

660
00:39:13,809 --> 00:39:15,227
she was killed.

661
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:19,148
I don't want the same thing
to happen to you.

662
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:31,577
You ruined the plan.
What were you thinking!?

663
00:39:33,662 --> 00:39:34,747
What's with that look?

664
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:38,084
Mori was just doing her job.

665
00:39:38,167 --> 00:39:39,251
What did you say?

666
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:44,840
Finding things that must not
be brought in,

667
00:39:44,924 --> 00:39:47,009
that's our job in Customs.

668
00:39:47,718 --> 00:39:48,928
Your results have nothing to do with it.

669
00:39:49,011 --> 00:39:50,763
Don't be so naive!

670
00:39:51,347 --> 00:39:53,641
That's why organized crime
takes advantage of you!

671
00:40:00,523 --> 00:40:01,565
Matsuyama.

672
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,069
Welcome

673
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:06,654
to Japan.

674
00:40:08,322 --> 00:40:09,240
What?

675
00:40:09,323 --> 00:40:11,075
Welcome to Japan.

676
00:40:12,451 --> 00:40:13,744
That's what I said

677
00:40:14,995 --> 00:40:17,039
when I welcomed Amita into this country.

678
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:19,417
But

679
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:21,919
right after that…

680
00:40:23,587 --> 00:40:26,715
her life was taken
by someone from this country.

681
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:31,470
Do you have

682
00:40:32,513 --> 00:40:35,975
any idea how deeply regrettable that is?

683
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:44,859
Don't think you'll get off easy for this.

684
00:40:47,570 --> 00:40:49,738
Are you going to fire me
using your authority?

685
00:40:50,406 --> 00:40:53,200
I've already submitted my resignation.

686
00:40:53,993 --> 00:40:55,244
Do as you like.

687
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:13,512
This morning, a report came in
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

688
00:41:14,138 --> 00:41:16,390
The person who received
the DVDs was arrested

689
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:19,477
and has reportedly confessed
to Amita's murder.

690
00:41:21,770 --> 00:41:23,230
Why did he…

691
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:29,236
The man invited Amita, who brought
the DVDs, for drinks, but she declined.

692
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:32,031
Enraged, he shoved her,

693
00:41:32,114 --> 00:41:33,824
and she fell and struck her head.

694
00:41:34,742 --> 00:41:35,951
Over something like that…

695
00:41:37,244 --> 00:41:39,663
Triggered by the man's statement,

696
00:41:39,747 --> 00:41:43,042
the crime group that planned to bring in
the classified info was also arrested.

697
00:41:44,752 --> 00:41:45,586
I see.

698
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:47,379
Now then…

699
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:52,551
…what do we do with this?

700
00:41:53,802 --> 00:41:55,471
NOTICE OF RESIGNATION

701
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:02,228
On a Chatwan news site,

702
00:42:02,311 --> 00:42:04,813
there was an article about a Japanese
researcher at a medical equipment firm

703
00:42:04,897 --> 00:42:08,275
being arrested for leaking
classified information.

704
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:10,444
The researcher sold classified information

705
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:13,948
to a Japanese organized crime group
to cover debts.

706
00:42:14,031 --> 00:42:17,451
And they tried to record that
onto a DVD and bring it in.

707
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:19,912
But why go through
the trouble of using a DVD?

708
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:22,706
Customs checks
on USB flash drives are strict,

709
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:25,834
which is why I think they recorded it
on a DVD, an older storage medium.

710
00:42:31,006 --> 00:42:32,341
Um, everyone--

711
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:36,303
-It'll be hard to replace you.
-True.

712
00:42:36,387 --> 00:42:38,055
-Chief, actually--
-We

713
00:42:38,138 --> 00:42:41,392
all apologize. We were
wrong to suspect you.

714
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:44,979
Let me say one last thing.

715
00:42:46,063 --> 00:42:47,815
We went through a lot together.

716
00:42:47,898 --> 00:42:50,734
Looking back, you were
an excellent customs officer.

717
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,778
-Thank you for everything.
-No, um--

718
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:56,824
Sorry for thinking you have such a naive
baby face, you can't handle this job.

719
00:42:56,907 --> 00:42:59,451
-Right?
-No, that's not what I--

720
00:42:59,535 --> 00:43:01,287
Everyone, please listen. I--

721
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,622
You decided not to quit, didn't you?

722
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:09,253
Counselor Sugihara called a moment ago.

723
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:13,799
After receiving this much care,
quitting isn't an option, is it?

724
00:43:17,678 --> 00:43:18,721
Here.

725
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:20,973
What is this?

726
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:22,683
Classified information.

727
00:43:32,901 --> 00:43:34,528
‎TO THE MISTER

728
00:43:40,075 --> 00:43:43,704
Mister, sorry for calling you lame
the other day.

729
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:48,292
Thank you for working hard to protect us.

730
00:43:49,335 --> 00:43:52,421
-You got this!
-You got this!

731
00:43:52,504 --> 00:43:56,008
-You got this!
-You got this!

732
00:44:02,264 --> 00:44:04,725
I thought they were just annoying kids…

733
00:44:06,185 --> 00:44:07,686
They were really paying attention

734
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:09,563
to our work, huh?

735
00:44:12,024 --> 00:44:13,692
Our job is opening people's luggage,

736
00:44:14,526 --> 00:44:15,986
taking away bad stuff,

737
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:19,281
with people angry at you.

738
00:44:19,948 --> 00:44:20,949
But

739
00:44:22,284 --> 00:44:24,244
if that protects someone…

740
00:44:26,538 --> 00:44:28,374
it's not a bad job, right?

741
00:44:38,175 --> 00:44:39,510
Welcome back.

742
00:44:44,723 --> 00:44:48,018
‎Hundrends of millions of yen worth
‎of drugs are about to be carried in.

743
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:51,063
‎We have to inspect the urn…

744
00:44:51,146 --> 00:44:52,523
‎What if we don't find anything?

745
00:44:52,606 --> 00:44:54,233
‎Women don't lie.

746
00:44:54,316 --> 00:44:55,901
‎What else could you be suspecting me of?

747
00:44:55,984 --> 00:44:57,903
‎We sincerely apologize to you.

748
00:44:57,986 --> 00:44:59,029
‎This is going to be a big problem.

749
00:44:59,113 --> 00:44:59,988
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
